From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:08:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compile the partial aggregate pushdown's assert-only check only when asserts are on

Assert-only code in partial_aggregate_pushdown.cpp binds values that only D_ASSERT()
reads, so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, the
bindings are unused and -Wunused-variable or -Wunused-but-set-variable
say so. The assert-only lines are compiled only when assertions are
enabled, with the side-effecting call kept in both builds, which is the
shape upstream gives the file later.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/optimizer/partial_aggregate_pushdown.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/partial_aggregate_pushdown.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/partial_aggregate_pushdown.cpp
index 0c767ee85d..d06e4bb5de 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/partial_aggregate_pushdown.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/partial_aggregate_pushdown.cpp
@@ -796,8 +796,12 @@ static unique_ptr<LogicalAggregate> DECreateUpperAggregate(Optimizer &optimizer,
 	for (auto &group : aggr.groups) {
 		auto &ref = group->Cast<BoundColumnRefExpression>();
 		idx_t gs;
+#ifdef D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED
 		auto has_side = GetExpressionSide(*group, side_bindings, gs);
 		D_ASSERT(has_side);
+#else
+		GetExpressionSide(*group, side_bindings, gs);
+#endif
 		auto binding = sides[gs].group_map.at(ref.Binding());
 		upper_aggr->groups.push_back(make_uniq<BoundColumnRefExpression>(ref.GetReturnType(), binding));
 	}
